cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these materials, cite this versioned research artifact and the
  accompanying manuscript. GitHub provides the source and complete release archive.
type: software
title: >-
  State Aggregation in Dynamic Graph Recovery: Separating Structural Ranking
  from Temporal Discrimination - Reproducibility Artifact
authors:
  - family-names: Chang
    given-names: Xuansong
    affiliation: Stony Brook Institute at Anhui University, Hefei, China
    email: alec.xs.chang@gmail.com
version: v2026.10.27.1
date-released: '2026-10-27'
repository-code: https://github.com/xschang1002/latent-state-graph-recovery
url: https://github.com/xschang1002/latent-state-graph-recovery/releases/tag/v2026.10.27.1
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code, simulation inputs and retained fitted outputs for the study of state
  aggregation in dynamic graph recovery. The evaluation separates pooled
  structural ranking, within-edge state discrimination and boundary detection.
  Includes paired duration and schedule studies; a separately specified
  symmetric-generator/window study; fixed shrinkage and residual controls;
  standard and positive-change AP and threshold sensitivity; a PELT segment-refit
  comparator; selected same-seed fresh-fitting checks; and auxiliary evidence.
  Current scientific guidance is in docs/research_guide.md, with dated protocols
  and execution provenance retained separately. MIT applies to project code;
  third-party components retain their own notices and conditions.
keywords:
  - dynamic graph recovery
  - temporal state discrimination
  - boundary-slot detection
  - state aggregation
  - reproducibility
